# Amigo Agents API Key Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and populate your actual API keys.
# NEVER commit .env to source control!

# 🔬 Amigo-Researcher (Claude / Anthropic API)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your_anthropic_api_key_here

# 🛡️ Amigo-Gatekeeper (Gemini / Google AI API)
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# 🔨 Amigo-Builder (Codex / OpenAI API)
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

# --- Optional: run Amigo-Gatekeeper on Kimi K3 (Moonshot API) ---
# The Gatekeeper runs on Gemini by default. Kimi is strictly opt-in: it is only
# used when GATEKEEPER_PROVIDER is set to "kimi" (case-insensitive), and that
# also requires MOONSHOT_API_KEY. Leave GATEKEEPER_PROVIDER unset -- or set it
# to "gemini" -- to keep the default provider. MOONSHOT_MODEL is only needed to
# pin a model id other than kimi-k3.
# GATEKEEPER_PROVIDER=kimi
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=your_moonshot_api_key_here
# MOONSHOT_MODEL=kimi-k3

# --- Optional: quota/rate-limit fallback endpoints (RAID I15) ---
# When a provider raises a quota/rate-limit error (HTTP 429), each role can
# retry once against an OpenAI/Anthropic-API-compatible fallback endpoint
# (e.g. a local LocalAI instance) instead of failing the whole run. The base
# URL, model, AND API key must all be set for a role's fallback to activate;
# leave all three commented out (the default) to keep today's fail-fast
# behavior. The fallback API key is required and kept separate from the
# primary key above -- the primary provider's real key is never sent to the
# fallback endpoint, since that endpoint may not be operated by the same
# trusted party.
# A fallback only re-points the primary provider's own client, so its endpoint
# must speak that provider's protocol: with GATEKEEPER_PROVIDER on gemini the
# URL must serve Gemini REST (google-genai never requests /chat/completions),
# and on kimi it must serve OpenAI chat-completions.
# RESEARCHER_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
# RESEARCHER_FALLBACK_MODEL=your-local-fallback-model
# RESEARCHER_FALLBACK_API_KEY=your-local-fallback-api-key
# BUILDER_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
# BUILDER_FALLBACK_MODEL=your-local-fallback-model
# BUILDER_FALLBACK_API_KEY=your-local-fallback-api-key
# GATEKEEPER_FALLBACK_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080/v1
# GATEKEEPER_FALLBACK_MODEL=your-local-fallback-model
# GATEKEEPER_FALLBACK_API_KEY=your-local-fallback-api-key
